# Backend Conventions

- Every query touching organization-scoped data (Branch,
  ShiftRequirement, and anything joined from them) MUST filter by the
  current user's organizationId, read from the JWT — never trust an
  organizationId passed in a request body or query string.
- Auth is JWT in an httpOnly cookie, issued only by
  /backend/src/routes/auth.ts. Both email/password and Google OAuth
  (Passport.js) must issue the cookie through the same helper function
  — never duplicate JWT-signing logic.
- Cookie settings branch on NODE_ENV: `SameSite=None; Secure` in
  production (frontend and backend are on different domains), `Lax`
  in local dev. CORS must have `credentials: true` and an explicit
  origin (never `*`) whenever cookies are involved.
- Routes under /api/public/* (the worker-facing availability
  submission and schedule-lookup endpoints) are intentionally
  unauthenticated. They must: (1) be rate-limited via
  express-rate-limit, (2) never return data belonging to a different
  ShiftRequirement than the one identified by linkToken, (3) never
  leak other workers' submissions to the requester.
- The scheduler module (/backend/src/scheduler/) has no database
  access — it's a pure function taking plain data in, returning an
  assignment result. Database reads/writes around it stay in the
  route handler, not inside the scheduler module.
- HiGHS is loaded once at server startup as a singleton — never
  re-initialize the WASM module inside a request handler.
